@title Cooling what-if: conditions, ranked fixes with a before and after table, 3D preview, apply
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The hot cabinet fixture opened in 3D. The Heat panel's "Cooling what-if" button opens the wizard beside the cabinet with the MODEL badge and two questions (hottest day, duty). "Try the fixes" runs the model and lists the fixes ranked; the first is picked and previewed in 3D with its before and after table. Applying puts the fix in the project (moves as one undo step, openings in Vents and fans).
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
# Opening Heat starts an automatic run: stop it, switch Auto off so it does not restart, and stop again.
click_text Cancel
wait 10
click_text Auto #1
wait 10
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 20
shot heat-panel
click_text "Cooling what-if"
wait 20
expect "Cooling what-if"
expect "MODEL, NOT MEASURED"
expect "Hottest day outside"
expect "Duty"
shot conditions
check_layout
click_text "Try the fixes"
wait_s 120
expect "Devices over limit"
expect "Tightest margin"
expect "Hottest air"
expect "Model estimate"
shot ranked-and-previewed
check_blank ranked-and-previewed
check_layout
# The window is shorter at 1366 and taller at 1920: scroll its list at the height where it sits in each.
scroll 250 420 -420
scroll 250 800 -420
wait 10
shot ranked-scrolled
click_text "Copy the table"
wait 6
expect "The table is on the clipboard."
try click_text "Apply the moves"
try click_text "Add the openings to Vents and fans"
wait 20
shot applied
check_layout
